From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: keanu-stitch8 <riski.aditia@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:57:34 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] nvn-mtl: a clear covers every layer of the bound render
 target view

NVN clears every layer of the render target view that is bound (the whole
texture when the view sets no layer range). A clear folded into a Metal
pass's load action clears only the layers the pass attaches, and a pass
that is not layered attaches one, so the other layers of an array, cube or
3D target kept their old or zero content.

Little Nightmares (01002FC00412C000, Unreal Engine 4) clears the 512x512
cube of each point light's one-pass shadow (geometry shader
ffc21034b958840b) in the pass that captures the vertex shader's output,
which is not layered. Only the +X face was cleared; faces 1-5 kept the zero
depth they were created with, every fragment the layered pass drew there
failed the depth test, and the comparison sampler read them as fully
shadowed: the lantern and the lighter lit only one side of the room, with
straight edges.

rp_begin_ex_ now clears such an attachment in a pass of its own with
renderTargetArrayLength set to the view's layers (att_layers), then loads
it in the real pass, as it already did for attachments larger than the
pass. A view limited to some layers clears only those; layered passes and
single-layer targets are unchanged. t_clear_layers runs the production
replay on a cube depth target and a 2D array colour target, with and
without layer ranges (4 of its 6 cases fail without the fix).

Checked on the Mac: Little Nightmares' shadow cube holds depth on all six
faces after the fix (texraw), and the lantern room is lit all around with
Six's shadow on the floor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#808
Reason: Little Nightmares' point lights lit one side of a room only: a clear of a layered target in a pass that is not layered covered layer 0 alone
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#328

